Proposals for all academic centers and institutes shall originate with faculty representing the disciplines, departments, schools, and/or colleges concerned. A proposal for the creation of an academic center or institute shall form its charter and include the following:
a detailed explanation of the Academic Center’s or Institute’s mission, goals, and rationale;
a thorough listing of the units that will participate in the proposed Academic Center’s or Institute’s governance, funding, and benefits;
the selection of a single college or school that will be the proposed Academic Center’s or Institute’s budgetary home;
a description of the proposed Academic Center’s or Institute’s administrative and staffing structure.
a detailed budget with thorough explanation of amounts of internal and external funding and their sources among the participating units, and including personnel and space requirements;
